WEBVTT

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.940
<b>The Killers Gather in the Wasteland</b>

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.860
<b>Wow, an actual fight.</b>

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.070
<b>Lupin dies tonight!</b>

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.450
<b>Hey, let's bet on who's gonna 
put Lupin down!</b>

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.460
Ready to die, Lupin III?

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.700
Wanna know what I'm
 thinking about right now?

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.960
How best to beg for mercy?

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.590
Which sweet young thing
 I'm taking to bed tonight.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.010
You talk big!

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.590
But spouting off's all 
you're good for, Lupin III!

00:02:08.630 --> 00:02:09.560
Amy!

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.890
We need to skedaddle, Amy.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:16.150
It's Ami.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.330
{now from bottom to top order}

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.410
<b>Lupin dies tonight!</b>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.410
<b>Hey, let's bet on who's gonna 
put Lupin down!</b>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.410
<b>Lupin's on the run.</b>

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.910
<b>As if he can get away on foot LOL</b>

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:28.160
<b>Hey, hitmen! He's in front of the fountain!</b>

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.470
He's by the fountain.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.660
Bring us around.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:36.000
There's practically 
a live feed on this guy.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.290
This'll be the easiest kill ever.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:39.970
<b>Lupin, no enemies to the east.</b>

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:40.720
<b>That's a lie</b>

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.930
<b>Whatever. Could you just die already?</b>

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.180
<b>But if Lupin bites the dust, that 
means the game ends</b>

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.050
<b>In that case, hang in there, Lupin!</b>

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.300
These guys seriously just write 
whatever pops into their heads!

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.090
Hey, Amy...

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:53.390
Oh, I'm with you now.

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.900
{bottom to top again}

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:57.990
<b>But if Lupin bites the dust, that 
means the game ends</b>

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:57.990
<b>In that case, hang in there, Lupin!</b>

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:57.990
<b>They went into the factory</b>

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.030
<b>Trapped like rats</b>

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.570
<b>So let's take bets on how Lupin's gonna die</b>

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.320
Surround the building.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.090
The Rat Clan...

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.810
They're relying on greater 
numbers to get it done.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.570
Wrong move. Speed's the key.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.980
And since all the best kills
 happen at night...

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.100
Hello, Underworld.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:26.590
Open German CPS. Enter default 
admin user name and password.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.480
Where are you hiding, Lupin?

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:43.730
I can already smell the stench of death.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.410
<b>Trapped like rats</b>

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.410
<b>So let's take bets on how Lupin's gonna die</b>

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.410
<b>What's going on in there?</b>

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.040
<b>Can't the drone get inside?</b>

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.250
<b>Can't they kill each other 
out where we can see them?!</b>

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:56.690
We see you hidin' there, missy!

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.410
Discharge.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.460
Lupin!

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.070
Run fire alarm system test.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:24.690
<i>Fire detected. Fire detected.
 This is just a system test.</i>

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.700
<i>Fire detected. Fire detected.
 This is just a system test.</i>

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.450
Stop your yapping. 
They're just playing mind games.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.980
Cheap tricks...

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.410
Stop!

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.890
We made the right move by not rushing in.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:56.970
Here he comes!

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.890
Gotta love that so-new-it's-not-
fully-assembled-yet car smell!

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.300
Move aside.

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:14.740
Amy!

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.660
He got away.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.250
No need to panic.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:34.260
It's not like he can leave the country.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:37.390
<b>Looks like Lupin was one step ahead.</b>

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:37.390
<b>Where'd he get that car?! 
What a cheater (mad)</b>

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:37.390
<b>The peeps betting Lupin would 
die are so salty right now, lolol</b>

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.230
<b>And that's the end of Round 1.</b>

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:39.020
<b>Did Jigen get away, too?</b>

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.270
Inspector, where are you going?

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.020
To Bwanda.

00:05:44.380 --> 00:05:46.630
But, sir, Bwanda's not an ICPO—

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.770
I realize that!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.910
<b>Vacation Request</b>

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.430
A vacation request?

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.420
I'm free to go where I like 
during my time off, aren't I?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.420
Oh, well. It's only a matter of time.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.460
In a tiny country like that, 
with that many hitmen on his trail,

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.280
there's no way he can escape.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.720
<b>And if even if he does, the ICPO 
will be after him again.</b>

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:08.930
<b>Either way, he's boxed in.</b>

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.150
Serves you right, Lupin III!

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:32.860
This is gonna hurt.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.560
Ow!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.790
The pain is proof that you are still alive.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.290
Let's chat for a bit. It'll help to distract you.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.910
Sounds unscientific...

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.950
I haven't felt pain like this... 
in a long time.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.580
Not since <i>they</i> kidnapped me.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.490
Who are "they"?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:55.980
When I was six, I was abducted 
by child pornographers.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:10.770
After they'd taken the pictures they 
wanted, we lived in conditions

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:13.120
that weren't even fit for livestock, 
waiting for someone to buy us.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.080
I'm still listening.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.620
But my tech skills saved me.

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:29.790
What are you brats doin'?!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.180
You made this?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.820
This might make us even 
more dough than the porn.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:53.410
I spent every day after 
that writing source code.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.610
Missing deadlines meant
 beatings, so I worked fast.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:02.050
And one of the things you cooked up 
was Marco Polo's payment system?

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:07.280
When I was 14, I managed to escape, 
and holed up in the Twin Towers.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.550
Not that my quality of 
life improved much...

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:11.420
That hurts!

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.840
She's asleep.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:23.320
I feel bad about this whole thing.

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:28.690
If only I'd been a bit more careful...

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.630
Are you in any position to worry 
about anyone other than yourself?

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.830
What the hell brought out the 
assassin all-stars in the first place?

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.390
A website for hitmen.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.760
Though, I'm just going off what 
my adoring public is telling me.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:46.960
But these guys know absolutely 
<i>everything</i> when it comes to Lupin III!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.700
That's rich, coming from the man himself.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:52.360
Lupin, I will leave our plan up to you.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.970
But I want to clear up one thing now: 
do we fight, or do we flee?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:57.530
Oh, that's an easy one.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:59.400
We take 'em all down.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:20.740
So I hear the entire Rat Clan let 
Lupin slip through their fingers...

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.860
And your people failed to take out Goemon.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.740
Ichiro, be a dear and settle down.

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:31.840
Here we go. Lupin's online.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.760
<i>Hey! Calling all hit-morons!</i>

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.330
<i>Taking you on one-by-one 
will take too long!</i>

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:39.130
<i>I'm gonna deal with you 
all at once, so bring it!</i>

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:42.390
I'm at the ruins of the 
Nudabale Tribe's old town!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.260
Come and get me!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:45.430
<b>I've seen that place before</b>

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:45.520
<b>Hey, hitdudes, you watching this? LOL</b>

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:45.520
<b>It's gonna be a battle royale!</b>

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.270
<b>So who's gonna come out on top?</b>

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:46.890
<b>Sweet, it's like a game</b>

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:47.770
<b>Duh, it's the Lupin Game</b>

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:54.120
Watson says there's no tech in the Nudabale 
ruins that Lupin's hacker can control.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:57.370
So he can't pull the same 
crap he did at the factory.

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.360
Look alive, boys!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.080
<b>Lupin seems pretty confident</b>

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:04.950
<b>I bet he's got some kind of plan</b>

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.830
<b>I reckon a giant robot's gonna burst out of the ground lol</b>

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:07.580
<b>Uh, no LOL</b>

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:07.920
<b>ROFL</b>

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.860
There's no way he'd pull that off.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.760
This is the real world.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:17.170
<b>Then why do you suppose
 he's pulling this stunt?</b>

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:17.170
It's obvious. He's desperate.

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:24.670
You're definitely going, then, Fujiko?

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:29.840
When it comes to <i>this</i> game, I doubt anyone 
in the world is better at it than me.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:38.820
Are you still in pain?

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.190
Not enough to affect my work.

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:43.830
Are you worried about me?

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.450
Hey! Here they come!

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:54.700
Well, well, well! And all those vehicles
have hired killers in them, huh?

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.290
Lupin's up there!

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:00.460
Kill him!

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:03.910
Load facial recognition system.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.930
Cross-check all faces with the databases 
on the deep web to identify them.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.460
The woman is Mama from the Union.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:12.230
Next to her are Ichiro and Lucky. 
One uses a fishing rod, the other, bombs.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:16.200
That's Akaki. He wields 
a transparent gun and knife.

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:16.780
<b>I bet a giant robot's gonna burst out of the ground lol</b>

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:16.780
<b>Uh, no LOL</b>

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:16.780
<b>ROFL</b>

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.360
<b>Make the battle royale 100x more interesting:</b>

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:20.110
<b>Assassin Ranking</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.370
<b>Newt</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.490
<b>Lucky</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.950
<b>Dr. Franken</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.070
<b>Chishio Akaki</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.660
<b>Shinpei Mayama</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.740
<b>King</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:24.830
<b>Black Viper</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Assassin Ranking</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>The Rat Clan's Chief</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Ichiro</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Kinkaku</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Ginkaku</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Sherdog</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Jukan Yorozuya</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Union Mama</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Captain Bone</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Ginbae</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Guardsman</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Flea</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>The Rat Clan</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Ani</b>

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Honcho</b>

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:23.320
<b>Whoa, this is amazing</b>

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:23.870
<b>It's like a roster</b>

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:24.700
<b>Good job on the website</b>

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.830
<b>I'm betting on the Rat Clan. 
Seems like there's a lot of them.</b>

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:27.450
<b>Naturally, I'm going
with Union Mama.</b>

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:29.730
I'd better be on my way.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:33.330
It'd be a shame if no one went to
 welcome our guests to the party.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.510
Right. Stick to the plan, guys!

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.460
Okay, here's the plan.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.930
This betting pool lets people 
bet on what day I'll die.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.850
Or in other words, on what day they'll kill me.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.350
But what if multiple people 
bet on the same day?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.480
They split the pot?

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:54.270
And no one wants that, 
so they all bet on different days.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.470
What are the people who 
attacked us after, then?

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:01.990
I figure they want to nab me and kill me
 on the day only <i>they've</i> bet on.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:06.990
Makes sense. They're making sure no one 
else kills you on a different date.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:11.130
In other words, you have two 
types of players in this game...

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:16.990
The ones who want to kill me, 
and the ones who want to catch me.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:22.060
That's why the Rat Clan 
shot Amy, and not me.

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:32.920
What's Lupin up to?

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.450
He hasn't made any kind of move yet...

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.270
Ah, now he is.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.490
<i>Here's our first tip!</i>

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:42.310
<i>Entry #4: The brothers, Kinkaku and Ginkaku.</i>

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:44.270
<i>They've put a bet on today 
being the day they kill me.</i>

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.500
What's this?

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.530
What's going on here, bro?

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.280
Shoot her, Ginkaku!

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.440
What all this means is, the biggest threat 
in this game is anyone who might kill me...

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.160
before the others can kidnap me.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.370
Die!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.670
This is crazy! The bets were
all supposed to be anonymous!

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:12.730
Watson says it's pretty likely he's got that 
girl who hacked the factory with him.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:16.430
Good work, like always, Amy.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:21.330
This assassination site has so much security,
 I'd say they're the paranoid type.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:23.080
Even I'm not able to break into it that fast.

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:24.700
Then, that means...

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.540
I'm bluffing.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:30.690
But without anyone to confirm otherwise, 
it sounds convincing enough.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.650
Girl, you've got what it takes!

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:39.610
I'm not interested in becoming a thief.

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:44.670
Nah.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:47.220
I mean, to survive in the real world.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.720
They're dropping like flies...

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.350
How many are left now?

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.710
This is bad.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:53.600
Don't let him deceive you.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.340
This is one of Lupin's schemes.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.560
I'll stick to the plan and 
head straight for Lupin.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.910
If you're trying to make your 
way up, this is a shortcut.

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:11.600
Daisuke Jigen!

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:18.450
Not that I'd ever let you take it.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:20.420
<b>Akaki's down</b>

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.130
<b>Aw, I was rooting for him</b>

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:21.710
<b>It's gonna be Ichiro from the Union</b>

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:34.700
Now, there's one other person who 
put money on my death happening today!

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:37.360
Who out of these three could it be?

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:37.980
<b>It's a quiz now?</b>

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:38.480
<b>He's just doing whatever 
he feels like</b>

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:39.190
<b>But it's fun to watch</b>

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.160
<b>There goes the Flea!</b>

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:51.660
<b>I was rooting for him</b>

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:52.410
<b>Hey! Ichiro killed another one!</b>

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.530
Can I ask you something?

00:14:54.810 --> 00:14:57.300
Anything you like, Princess Internet.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.540
Which "sweet young thing" did you take to bed?

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:02.780
You're seriously asking me that?

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:06.790
I've been thinking about it for a while, 
but I can't come up with an answer.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:10.520
I have a hard time understanding how 
your mind could have been on women

00:15:10.520 --> 00:15:12.550
at a time like that in the first place.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:16.110
It was already late.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:18.050
Were you talking about a call girl?

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:19.180
<b>And another one bites the dust</b>

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:19.850
<b>That was Guardsman</b>

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:19.850
<b>Dammit, I lose</b>

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:20.440
<b>Lupin's gang is pretty tough</b>

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.900
Could either Jigen or Goemon 
actually be a woman?

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:24.920
Okay, that's just plain weird.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.780
Did you intend on sleeping with me, then?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:30.360
Why? Do you want me to?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.690
I <i>am</i> interested.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:37.060
Since I've never had sex before.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.950
Well, hard luck. I only sleep with adults.

00:15:41.470 --> 00:15:43.590
Like Fujiko Mine?

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:49.440
Where did you hear that name?

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.990
It came up in the search algorithm.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:57.250
She's one of your known associates, 
along with Jigen and Goemon.

00:15:57.250 --> 00:16:00.100
There are also rumors that 
she's your girlfriend.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.110
That info's way out of date.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:07.130
It's not like that between 
Fujiko and me anymore.

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:19.410
<b>The field's really thinning out.</b>

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.160
<b>Who's in first place?</b>

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:20.790
<b>Union Mama's Ichiro.</b>

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.620
<b>He's taken out five people already.</b>

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:28.120
I'll take Goemon down first, Mama.

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:41.380
He's stronger than he was before, Mama!

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:43.650
But even so...

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.150
I got him, Mama!

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.940
One tug on this line and
 his head goes flying!

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:58.160
And I win!

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:00.670
How do you plan on doing 
that in your condition?

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:05.960
<b>Ichiro's down!</b>

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:06.580
<b>Dammit, I lose</b>

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.290
<b>Who's even left?</b>

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:11.800
Even killing every assassin 
here won't end this.

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.870
The bounty's still on the website.

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:19.600
You'll still be hunted.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:20.800
Yeah, probably.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:24.880
Why don't you just retire?

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:28.330
With your talent for disguises, 
you could live a quiet life.

00:17:28.950 --> 00:17:31.880
Another one of your logical 
conclusions, huh?

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.160
Sorry, but that's just not how I...

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:37.690
Hey, we finally have a visitor.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.370
<b>That's the head of the Rat Clan.</b>

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:47.870
<b>Nice one, chief.</b>

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:48.330
<b>It's a showdown</b>

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:49.210
<b>Now, things are getting juicy!</b>

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:01.810
You're the only one who made it?

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:06.140
Lupin, I'm not here for the bounty anymore.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:11.730
In the name of my fallen clan 
members, I will kill you.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.050
Sounds like a plan.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:18.490
I owe you for what you did to 
my logistics agent, anyway.

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:58.000
Sorry, but I've never seen 
the appeal of playing fair.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:04.150
Oh, yeah! I win!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:04.660
<b>It's a showdown</b>

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:04.660
<b>Now, things are getting juicy!</b>

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:05.330
<b>Lupin's a badass</b>

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:05.950
<b>Isn't that cheating?</b>

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:06.450
<b>Well played, Lupin</b>

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:06.790
<b>Bring on the next assassin, quick~</b>

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:16.540
Damn, that's good.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.800
Today was a good day.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:27.310
See? Men need foes.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.430
That makes no sense.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.490
Foes to surpass. Foes to oppose.

00:19:32.490 --> 00:19:35.700
Rivals, friends, parents, women...

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:37.970
Women are foes?

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:40.450
The most puzzling and 
precious foes you can have!

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:51.960
Another killer?

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.550
Hey, Fujiko.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:15.760
Were you that worried about me?

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.080
Of course not.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:20.630
You know <i>I'd</i> never be the 
one chasing <i>you</i>, silly.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.110
Hey, I'm not chasing you, either.

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.860
Didn't you steal me on my wedding day once?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:30.230
Well, a thief's job is to 
thieve things, after all.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.870
I don't remember asking you to.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:35.790
<b>And in walks the ex!</b>

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:36.540
<b>Lupin got dumped?</b>

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:36.960
<b>Poor guy</b>

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.380
<b>So we're moving from suspense 
to romance now, huh?</b>

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.620
I've got a present for you, Lupin.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.810
Your first one from me in four years.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:48.850
If anyone's gonna kill you,
 it should be me.

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:17.930
My name is Goemon Ishikawa.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:25.110
Zenigata is the man who pursues Lupin 
through scorching heat and crashing waves.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:28.870
And now, he and Lupin must flee 
into the desert together.

00:22:28.870 --> 00:22:32.200
Surely there must be a limit 
to one man's ardor...

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:37.990
With Lupin's life in danger, will his 
nemesis, Zenigata, do what he must?

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:41.300
Next time: "Zenigata's Pride
 and the Desert Dust."

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>Zenigata's Pride and the Desert Dust</b>

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:43.880
I wasn't trying to sound lyrical...
